# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Shell scripts MUST be LF — defense-in-depth against autocrlf=true (g-115-869).
# Without these explicit rules, `* text=auto` is heuristic-only and git's
# enforcement is not guaranteed; charlie's 2026-05-16 rc=127 incident (CRLF
# bash refusing to exec) reproduced because `_runtime.sh` was attr=text=auto,
# not attr=text eol=lf. Sibling fix: g-115-868 routes insight-trigger-sweep
# through _rt.py to bypass bash entirely.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Git hooks are shell scripts too, but EXTENSIONLESS — the *.sh/*.bash rules
# above don't match their names, so pin them to LF explicitly. autocrlf=true
# would otherwise check them out as CRLF on a fresh clone and break execution
# (same g-115-869 rc=127 class). Covers pre-commit/post-commit/pre-push and any
# future hook — critical because a fresh-clone machine (machine-2, CI) is exactly
# where the pre-push M2 tag gate must still run.
core/githooks/* text eol=lf
